{
  "scope": "CPU-only optional complete DD multiplication windows integrated into the retained LL14 product forest. Preserve keys, ciphertext coefficients, tree pairing, odd-leaf carries, scales, moduli, approximation and precision gates. Defaults remain unchanged.",
  "implementation_commit": "8b4e832",
  "replay_control_commit": "54797f1",
  "algorithm": "Borrow typed operand and output pointers from the forest; each eight-product window performs exact RNS tensors, auxiliary lift, shared-key gadget batch, auxiliary rounding, linear-term addition and final data scale down. Recurse with the original per-level keys and round/carry order. No ciphertext gather/scatter copies or input-dependent persistent state.",
  "compatibility": "Small-ring parameters keep the existing raw-key fallback when the prepared backend is not selected. The first unit attempt exposed an accidental change in this selection; the corrected implementation passes both raw and prepared cases.",
  "key_reuse": "The setup observer retains the already-created immutable level-chunk key chain. Independent and windowed replay callbacks capture the same shared object; there is no second prepared chain for the comparison and no evaluation-key encryption or generation.",
  "controls": {
    "enable": "--dd-windowed 1 requires --tensor-rns 1 --dd-wide-rns 1 --dd-primary-bits 40 --dd-level-chunks 1 --batch-product-trees 1 with fixed backends.",
    "pair": "--dd-windowed-pair 1: warm independent/windowed, then independent/windowed/windowed/independent. One function and separate paired controls.",
    "reports": "dd_windowed, dd_windowed_pair_warmup and dd_windowed_batch_calls record policy and dispatch. Tree/factor/tail-alignment wall times are accumulated from existing root-stage observations without another timer."
